# RegistryMirrorBlob5xxRate (homelab#1297) — lifted VERBATIM out of prometheusrule.yaml (comments
# AND annotations stripped — the manifest is its one home). The rules file that
# mirror-debug.promtool-test loads. Not a manifest and not applied to anything: `promtool test
# rules` needs upstream-format rules (top-level `groups:`), and a PrometheusRule keeps them under
# `.spec`, so the CR cannot be loaded directly. Named .promtool-rules rather than .yaml on purpose
# — manifest-lint kubeconforms EVERY *.yaml under argocd/resources and a non-manifest there would
# fail it.
#
# ANNOTATIONS ARE STRIPPED deliberately, following mirror-probes.promtool-rules: this pins FIRING
# BEHAVIOUR, not prose. The descriptions are runbooks and change on their own schedule; copying
# them here would give the runbook two homes.
#
# ⚠ THIS COPY IS NOT DRIFT-PINNED — same standing caveat as mirror-probes.promtool-rules. A stale
# copy tests the OLD expr and passes VACUOUSLY. Re-copy after editing this alert:
#
#   yq -o=json '{"groups": [{"name": "registry-cache", "rules": [.spec.groups[].rules[] | select(.alert == "RegistryMirrorBlob5xxRate") | del(.annotations)]}]}' \
#     argocd/resources/registry-cache/prometheusrule.yaml | yq -P '.'
#   (one line on purpose — a wrapped yq program string is the #344 lexer bug)
#
# DIRECTION WITNESS OMITTED: the existing mirror-probes.promtool-rules already proves the
# direction principle (min_over_time vs max_over_time) for this class. A max_over_time witness
# here would need a subquery (max_over_time(rate(...)[5m:1m])) which promtool does not support.
groups:
  - name: registry-cache
    rules:
      - alert: RegistryMirrorBlob5xxRate
        expr: rate(registry_http_requests_total{handler="blob", code=~"5.."}[5m]) > 0
        for: 10m
        labels:
          severity: warning